---
import BaseLayout from '@/layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
const updated = '3 September 2026';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Privacy Policy"
  description="How this site handles your data. Photos are processed entirely in your browser and never uploaded. This page explains what is and is not collected."
>
  <h1 class="text-3xl font-semibold tracking-tight text-ink-900">Privacy Policy</h1>
  <p class="mt-2 text-sm text-ink-400">Last updated {updated}</p>

  <div class="markdown mt-8 max-w-2xl">
    <h2>Your photographs</h2>
    <p>
      Photographs you open in this tool are never uploaded. Face detection, background
      separation, cropping and encoding all run inside your own browser using WebAssembly.
      No copy of your image is transmitted to this site's servers or to any third party, and
      no copy is stored anywhere after you close or reload the page.
    </p>
    <p>
      This is a property of how the tool is built, not a policy promise we ask you to take
      on trust. You can verify it: open your browser's developer tools, switch to the
      Network tab, and process a photo. You will see requests for the model files and
      nothing carrying your image.
    </p>

    <h2>What is collected</h2>
    <p>
      We do not ask you to create an account and we do not collect names, email addresses or
      any other personal details. Standard server logs may record the IP address, browser
      user agent and requested URL of visits, which is unavoidable in serving a website and
      is used only to keep the site running and to diagnose faults.
    </p>

    <h2>Advertising and cookies</h2>
    <p>
      This site displays advertising supplied by Google, which pays for its hosting. Google
      and its partners may set cookies or read existing ones to serve and measure ads, and
      may use your approximate location and browsing history to choose which ads to show.
      This happens through Google's advertising systems; we never pass your photograph or
      any image data to them, because we never have a copy to pass on.
    </p>
    <p>
      If you are in the European Economic Area, the United Kingdom or Switzerland, you will
      be asked for consent before any non-essential cookie is set, and you can change or
      withdraw that choice at any time. You can also review and adjust the ads you see at
      <a href="https://myadcenter.google.com/" rel="noopener" target="_blank">Google My Ad Center</a>,
      and opt out of personalised advertising from participating vendors at
      <a href="https://optout.aboutads.info/" rel="noopener" target="_blank">aboutads.info</a>.
    </p>

    <h2>Your rights</h2>
    <p>
      Because we hold no account and no photographs, there is normally no personal data of
      yours for us to show you, correct or delete. If you believe we hold something about
      you and want it removed, contact us and we will act on it.
    </p>

    <h2>Children</h2>
    <p>
      This site is not directed at children under 13 and we do not knowingly collect
      information from them. A parent making a passport photo for a child is of course
      welcome to use the tool; the photograph stays on their device like any other.
    </p>

    <h2>Changes</h2>
    <p>
      If this policy changes, the date at the top of this page changes with it. Material
      changes will be noted on the site.
    </p>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
